---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/ui/TldrBox.astro';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  // Sample blog posts - will be replaced with Keystatic content
  const posts = [
    {
      slug: 'fda-510k-clearance-process',
      title: 'Understanding FDA 510(k) Clearance for Medical Devices',
      description: 'A comprehensive guide to the FDA 510(k) clearance process for medical device manufacturers looking to enter the US market.',
      tldr: 'FDA 510(k) clearance requires demonstrating substantial equivalence to a predicate device. The process typically takes 3-6 months and involves quality system compliance, biocompatibility testing, and clinical data.',
      author: 'BRITZMEDI Team',
      publishedAt: '2025-12-15',
      updatedAt: '2025-12-20',
      category: 'education',
      tags: ['FDA', 'Regulatory', 'Medical Devices', '510(k)', 'US Market'],
      content: `
## What is FDA 510(k) Clearance?

The FDA 510(k) premarket notification is a regulatory pathway that allows medical device manufacturers to demonstrate that their device is substantially equivalent to a legally marketed predicate device.

### Key Requirements

1. **Substantial Equivalence**: Your device must have the same intended use and similar technological characteristics as a predicate device.

2. **Quality System Compliance**: Manufacturers must comply with FDA's Quality System Regulation (21 CFR Part 820).

3. **Documentation**: Comprehensive technical documentation including design controls, risk analysis, and verification/validation testing.

### Timeline and Process

The typical 510(k) review process takes 3-6 months:

- **Pre-submission Meeting** (Optional): 2-3 months before submission
- **Submission Preparation**: 2-4 months
- **FDA Review**: 90-180 days
- **Additional Information Requests**: Variable

### BRITZMEDI's FDA Journey

BRITZMEDI successfully obtained FDA 510(k) clearance (K212561) for the TORR RF Multi-Wave RF System in 2022. This clearance demonstrates our commitment to meeting the highest international regulatory standards.

## Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: How much does 510(k) clearance cost?**
A: Total costs typically range from $50,000 to $150,000, including testing, consulting, and FDA user fees.

**Q: Can I market my device during the review?**
A: No, you must wait for FDA clearance before marketing in the United States.

**Q: What's the difference between 510(k) and PMA?**
A: 510(k) is for devices substantially equivalent to existing devices, while PMA (Premarket Approval) is required for higher-risk Class III devices.
      `,
      faqs: [
        {
          question: 'How much does FDA 510(k) clearance cost?',
          answer: 'Total costs typically range from $50,000 to $150,000, including testing, consulting, and FDA user fees of approximately $13,000 for small businesses.'
        },
        {
          question: 'Can I market my device during the FDA review?',
          answer: 'No, you must wait for FDA clearance before marketing in the United States. Marketing without clearance can result in significant penalties.'
        },
        {
          question: 'What is the difference between 510(k) and PMA?',
          answer: '510(k) is for devices substantially equivalent to existing devices, while PMA (Premarket Approval) is required for higher-risk Class III devices and involves more extensive clinical testing.'
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      slug: 'rf-technology-aesthetic-medicine',
      title: 'RF Technology in Aesthetic Medicine: A 2025 Overview',
      description: 'Explore how radiofrequency technology is transforming aesthetic treatments with improved safety and efficacy.',
      tldr: 'Modern RF devices use multi-frequency technology for customized skin tightening treatments. Key innovations include real-time temperature monitoring and auto-circular motion for even energy delivery.',
      author: 'BRITZMEDI Team',
      publishedAt: '2025-11-28',
      category: 'technology',
      tags: ['RF Technology', 'Aesthetic Medicine', 'TORR RF', 'Skin Tightening'],
      content: `
## The Evolution of RF Technology

Radiofrequency technology has become a cornerstone of non-invasive aesthetic treatments. Modern devices offer precise energy delivery for skin tightening, body contouring, and collagen stimulation.

### Multi-Wave RF Technology

Traditional RF devices operate at a single frequency, limiting treatment customization. Multi-Wave RF technology, pioneered in devices like BRITZMEDI's TORR RF, offers:

- **Multiple Frequency Options**: 1MHz, 2MHz, and 4MHz for different treatment depths
- **Real-Time Temperature Control**: Ensures consistent treatment outcomes
- **Auto Circular Motion**: Patented technology for even energy distribution

### Clinical Applications

RF technology is used for various aesthetic indications:

1. Facial skin tightening and lifting
2. Body contouring and cellulite reduction
3. Vascular lesion treatment
4. Pain management and rehabilitation
      `,
      faqs: [
        {
          question: 'Is RF treatment painful?',
          answer: 'RF treatments are generally well-tolerated. Patients may feel warmth and mild pressure during treatment. Advanced devices include comfort features like vibration to minimize discomfort.'
        },
        {
          question: 'How many RF sessions are needed?',
          answer: 'Most patients see results after 3-6 sessions, spaced 1-2 weeks apart. Maintenance treatments every 3-6 months help sustain results.'
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      slug: 'korean-beauty-device-market',
      title: 'Korean Beauty Device Market: Global Expansion Trends',
      description: 'How Korean medical device manufacturers are leading innovation in the global aesthetic market.',
      tldr: 'Korean beauty device exports grew 23% in 2024. Key success factors include FDA/CE certifications, advanced R&D, and focus on non-invasive treatments.',
      author: 'BRITZMEDI Team',
      publishedAt: '2025-10-20',
      category: 'industry-news',
      tags: ['K-Beauty', 'Market Trends', 'Export', 'Medical Devices'],
      content: `
## Korean Beauty Device Industry Overview

South Korea has emerged as a global leader in aesthetic medical device manufacturing, combining advanced technology with innovative design.

### Market Growth Factors

- Strong government support for medical device R&D
- Established K-beauty brand recognition
- Focus on non-invasive treatment options
- Competitive manufacturing costs with high quality

### Export Success

Korean beauty device exports have shown consistent growth, with key markets including:

1. United States and Canada
2. European Union
3. Southeast Asia
4. Middle East
      `,
      faqs: []
    }
  ];

  return posts.map(post => ({
    params: { slug: post.slug },
    props: { post }
  }));
}

const { post } = Astro.props;

// Article structured data
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  'headline': post.title,
  'description': post.description,
  'author': {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    'name': post.author,
    'url': 'https://britzmedi.com'
  },
  'publisher': {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    'name': 'BRITZMEDI Co., Ltd.',
    'logo': {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      'url': 'https://britzmedi.com/logo.png'
    }
  },
  'datePublished': post.publishedAt,
  'dateModified': post.updatedAt || post.publishedAt,
  'mainEntityOfPage': {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `https://britzmedi.com/blog/${post.slug}`
  }
};

// FAQ structured data (if post has FAQs)
const faqSchema = post.faqs?.length > 0 ? {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  'mainEntity': post.faqs.map(faq => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    'name': faq.question,
    'acceptedAnswer': {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      'text': faq.answer
    }
  }))
} : null;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={post.title}
  description={post.description}
  keywords={post.tags}
>
  <!-- Article Structured Data -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />

  <!-- FAQ Structured Data (if applicable) -->
  {faqSchema && (
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  )}

  <article class="py-12 lg:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-500">
          <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-primary-600">Home</a></li>
          <li>/</li>
          <li><a href="/blog" class="hover:text-primary-600">Blog</a></li>
          <li>/</li>
          <li class="text-slate-700 truncate max-w-[200px]">{post.title}</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <!-- Article Header -->
        <header class="mb-10">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider bg-primary-100 text-primary-700 rounded-full">
              {post.category.replace('-', ' ')}
            </span>
            <time datetime={post.publishedAt} class="text-sm text-slate-500">
              {new Date(post.publishedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}
            </time>
          </div>

          <h1 class="heading-1 mb-6">{post.title}</h1>

          <p class="body-large text-slate-600 mb-8">
            {post.description}
          </p>

          <!-- TL;DR Box -->
          {post.tldr && (
            <TldrBox summary={post.tldr} class="mb-8" />
          )}

          <!-- Author and Share -->
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 py-6 border-y border-slate-200">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-primary-500 to-primary-700 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-semibold">
                B
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="font-medium text-slate-900">{post.author}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">BRITZMEDI Co., Ltd.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-500">Share:</span>
              <a
                href={`https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=https://britzmedi.com/blog/${post.slug}&title=${encodeURIComponent(post.title)}`}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="p-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors"
                aria-label="Share on LinkedIn"
              >
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-600" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433c-1.144 0-2.063-.926-2.063-2.065 0-1.138.92-2.063 2.063-2.063 1.14 0 2.064.925 2.064 2.063 0 1.139-.925 2.065-2.064 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
                </svg>
              </a>
              <a
                href={`https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=${encodeURIComponent(post.title)}&url=https://britzmedi.com/blog/${post.slug}`}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="p-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors"
                aria-label="Share on Twitter"
              >
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-600" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/>
                </svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Article Content -->
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-semibold prose-a:text-primary-600 prose-img:rounded-xl">
          <Fragment set:html={post.content.split('\n').map(line => {
            if (line.startsWith('## ')) return `<h2>${line.slice(3)}</h2>`;
            if (line.startsWith('### ')) return `<h3>${line.slice(4)}</h3>`;
            if (line.startsWith('**Q:')) return `<p class="font-semibold">${line}</p>`;
            if (line.startsWith('**A:')) return `<p>${line}</p>`;
            if (line.startsWith('- **')) return `<li><strong>${line.slice(4).split('**')[0]}</strong>: ${line.split('**')[2] || ''}</li>`;
            if (line.startsWith('- ')) return `<li>${line.slice(2)}</li>`;
            if (line.match(/^\d+\./)) return `<li>${line.slice(line.indexOf(' ') + 1)}</li>`;
            if (line.trim() === '') return '<br />';
            return `<p>${line}</p>`;
          }).join('')} />
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ Section (if applicable) -->
        {post.faqs?.length > 0 && (
          <section class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-slate-200">
            <h2 class="heading-2 mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <div class="space-y-6">
              {post.faqs.map((faq, index) => (
                <div class="card-premium p-6">
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3 text-slate-900">
                    {faq.question}
                  </h3>
                  <p class="body-base text-slate-600">
                    {faq.answer}
                  </p>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        )}

        <!-- Tags -->
        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {post.tags.map(tag => (
              <span class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 rounded-full">
                #{tag}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Back to Blog -->
        <div class="mt-12">
          <a
            href="/blog"
            class="inline-flex items-center text-primary-600 font-medium hover:text-primary-700"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
            </svg>
            Back to Blog
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
